# Reusable UI Components

Source of truth: `docs/design/theme-guide.md`, `Core/Theme/Components/`.

When building screens (chat, session list, settings, …), **compose shared components** — do not invent one-off styled views per screen or per message role.

## Hard rules

1. **One component, many configurations** — same shape for variants; pass a role / style / flag (e.g. `isUser`, `role: .accent`). Do **not** create `UserChatBubble` + `AssistantChatBubble`.
2. **Theme tokens only** — `Color.theme.*`, `Font.theme.*`, `Spacing.*`, `Radius.*`. Never raw hex, `Color.blue`, or `.font(.system(size:))` in Features or Components.
3. **Live in `Core/Theme/Components/`** — shared chrome (bubbles, buttons, fields, badges, cards). Feature screens only layout + wire ViewModel state into those components.
4. **Style changes stay in one place** — changing accent / surface / body font must update every consumer without editing Feature files.
5. **Copy via `L10n`** — user-visible strings use `L10n.*`, not English literals (see `Core/Localization/`).

## Canonical pattern — ChatBubble

User and assistant messages share **one** bubble; configuration drives look:

```swift
// ✅ Core/Theme/Components/ChatBubble.swift
struct ChatBubble: View {
    let text: String
    let isUser: Bool

    var body: some View {
        Text(text)
            .font(.theme.body)
            .foregroundStyle(isUser ? Color.theme.onAccent : Color.theme.textPrimary)
            .padding(.horizontal, Spacing.lg)
            .padding(.vertical, Spacing.md)
            .background(isUser ? Color.theme.accent : Color.theme.surface)
            // clip / alignment from isUser …
    }
}

// ✅ Features/Chat/ChatView.swift — compose, don't restyle
ForEach(viewModel.messages) { message in
    ChatBubble(text: message.content, isUser: message.isUser)
}
```

```swift
// ❌ Duplicate components / hardcoded colors in the feature
struct UserMessageView: View { /* blue #3478F6 … */ }
struct BotMessageView: View { /* gray … */ }
```

Same idea for buttons (`PrimaryButton` / `SecondaryButton`), badges (`ThemeBadge` + `role`), text fields (`ThemeTextField`), cards (`ThemeCard`).

## When adding UI

| Do | Don't |
|---|---|
| Extend or parameterize an existing theme component | Copy-paste padding/colors into `ChatView` / list rows |
| Add a `role` / `isUser` / style enum if a new variant appears | Fork a second nearly identical view |
| Put new shared chrome under `Core/Theme/Components/` | Bury reusable styling inside one Feature folder |
| Preview light + dark on the component | Only preview the full screen |

## Checklist before finishing a UI task

- [ ] Message / row / button variants share one component API
- [ ] Colors/fonts/spacing come from theme tokens
- [ ] Tweaking `Color.theme.accent` (or surface/body) visibly updates the new UI without Feature edits
- [ ] No parallel “user vs app” view types that only differ by color
